{"content":[{"c":["JEIEL"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":[" 1. Chief in Reuben’s tribe (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.5.7","r":"1Chr.5.7","rawR":"1Chr.5.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.5.7","value":"1Chr.5.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 5:7"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 2. Benjamite who lived at Gibeon and an ancestor of Israel’s first king, Saul (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.8.29","r":"1Chr.8.29","rawR":"1Chr.8.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.8.29","value":"1Chr.8.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 8:29"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.35","r":"1Chr.9.35","rawR":"1Chr.9.35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.35","value":"1Chr.9.35"}],"t":"ref","v":"9:35"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 3. One of David’s mighty men (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.11.44","r":"1Chr.11.44","rawR":"1Chr.11.44","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.11.44","value":"1Chr.11.44"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 11:44"},"). He is perhaps identical with #1 above."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 4. Levite gatekeeper in the sanctuary. He seems to have served as a musician also (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.15.18,21","r":"1Chr.15.18,21","rawR":"1Chr.15.18,21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.15.18,21","value":"1Chr.15.18,21"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 15:18, 21"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.16.5","r":"1Chr.16.5","rawR":"1Chr.16.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.16.5","value":"1Chr.16.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"16:5b"},"). The Jeiel of ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.16.5","r":"1Chr.16.5","rawR":"1Chr.16.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.16.5","value":"1Chr.16.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 16:5a"}," is probably a different musician."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 5. Levite descended from Asaph and an ancestor of a prophet named Jahaziel (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.20.14","r":"2Chr.20.14","rawR":"2Chr.20.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.20.14","value":"2Chr.20.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 20:14"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 6. Secretary for King Uzziah’s army, who kept or made military “rolls” or “musters” of the king’s troops (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.26.11","r":"2Chr.26.11","rawR":"2Chr.26.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.26.11","value":"2Chr.26.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 26:11"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 7. KJV and ",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," spelling of Jeuel, Elizaphan’s descendant, in ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.29.13","r":"2Chr.29.13","rawR":"2Chr.29.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.29.13","value":"2Chr.29.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chronicles 29:13"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Jeuel_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Jeuel_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Jeuel_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Jeuel #2"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 8. Levite leader who contributed Passover offerings during King Josiah’s reign (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.35.9","r":"2Chr.35.9","rawR":"2Chr.35.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.35.9","value":"2Chr.35.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 35:9"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 9. KJV spelling of Jeuel, Adonikam’s descendant, in ",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.8.13","r":"Ezra.8.13","rawR":"Ezra.8.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.8.13","value":"Ezra.8.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezra 8:13"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Jeuel_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Jeuel_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Jeuel_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Jeuel #3"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["10. Nebo’s descendant who was encouraged to divorce his foreign wife during the postexilic era (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.10.43","r":"Ezra.10.43","rawR":"Ezra.10.43","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.10.43","value":"Ezra.10.43"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 10:43"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Jeiel","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Chr 5:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_diction